WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.602
We joke in my household that

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:04.904
Michelle,

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.506
you know, she's got a dazzling smile.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:07.140
Yeah,

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.144
I mean,

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.113
and listen,

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.414
I understand

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.049
there's in terms of popularity,

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:18.785
there's basically Michelle

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.755
Malia, Sasha,

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.624
Sunny, our dog and me.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.126
I understand

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.561
she's hot,

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.630
she's smart.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:32.899
She is

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:35.702
she's charming.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.771
She's intelligent. I get it.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.806
But here here's here

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.274
here's a little secret about Michelle.

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:41.975
You know,

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:43.543
in our household,

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:45.245
she can be a little bit of

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.781
the glass half empty person sometimes.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:49.516
You know, she

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.450
she she can

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.785
she can get a little discouraged

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:54.888
about what she sees happening.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:55.922
And, you know, I'm

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.924
the hope and change there.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.125
So, I mean, I'm

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.761
usually a little more optimistic.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:04.397
And so if she's been watching the news

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.999
or reading the papers

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:08.735
and some crazy stuff is taking place,

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.236
which is basically every 10 minutes

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:13.640
you know,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.340
she she can get a

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.576
little down and I'll say, honey,

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.878
everything's going to be okay.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.414
And I believe that

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.350
I believe things will be okay.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.487
But I also know that things won't be okay

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.588
on their own.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.659
They'll be okay

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:35.628
if we make the effort.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.933
It'll be okay if we work for it,

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.101
not just on Election Day,

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.103
but every day in between.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:43.770
Right

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.610
And I know

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.845
look, I know some of you

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:53.012
probably feel like Michelle

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:53.880
does sometimes

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.682
because I feel even me, the hope

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:58.251
and change guy, I can get discouraged.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.387
Politics

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.857
is so nasty and mean and

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:07.127
it it just seems like

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.662
people will say anything and do anything.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:12.999
And it and it can be depressing

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.134
sometimes.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.504
And a lot of what we used to take

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:18.037
for granted,

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.707
things like

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.276
respect and common decency

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.878
and telling the truth

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:26.513
and believing in science

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.681
and the idea that every vote should count

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:29.582
and that the person

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.718
with the most votes win

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:34.721
all that somehow

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:37.590
has become controversial

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:39.893
but

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:43.730
I was listening backstage with Josh,

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.031
talked about

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.000
the experience

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:47.634
of him

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.535
running for governor

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:50.303
and traveling around the state,

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.705
and it reminded me of the experience

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.274
that I had first as a state

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:56.042
senator traveling around my district

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:58.111
and then as a U.S.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.412
Senate candidate in Illinois

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.314
and then as a presidential candidate

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:01.948
it's a it's

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:04.050
such a privilege to be able to

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.152
to meet people from every walk of life

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:06.686
be folks

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.588
who look different and

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.790
and live in different places.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:11.524
And

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:15.161
and it would always remind me

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:17.430
and what

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:20.466
we have to remind ourselves

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.569
is that there's this common thread.

00:03:22.569 --> 00:03:26.339
There's this thing that binds us together

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:28.141
as Americans,

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.810
a belief that no matter who we are

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.878
or where we come from,

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:32.779
what we look like,

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:33.479
who we love,

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.682
what our last name is, how we worship

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.652
a belief that all of us matter

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.556
the kind of slash and burn

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.093
politics that we're seeing right now

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.095
that doesn't have to be who we are.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.432
We can be better.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:54.601
And it has nothing to do,

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.669
by the way, with political correctness

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.605
or being to walk.

00:03:58.605 --> 00:04:00.840
It's about fundamental values

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.141
that my grandparents

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:05.311
from Kansas taught me, values I grew up

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:08.381
with, values you grew up with, values.

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:11.084
We try to teach our kids values.

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:12.552
We learn in churches

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:15.722
and mosques and synagogues and temples.

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:18.958
Honesty, fairness, opportunity.

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:21.961
Hard work values that Josh Shapiro

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:24.330
and John Spellman stand for.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:25.531
Values.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.933
The Joe Biden

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:30.303
stands for values that were enshrined

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.338
in our founding documents

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:34.240
a few miles from here,

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.710
a clarion call for freedom and equality

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:39.579
that Philly's own Liberty

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:40.680
Bell represents.

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:42.482
That's

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:45.618
what America stands for.

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:49.522
That's who we are

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:51.891
So if you're anxious

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.994
and frustrated right now, don't complain,

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.563
don't mope,

00:04:57.864 --> 00:04:59.766
don't tune out

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.601
get off your couch.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.802
And do what?

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.772
Put down your phones and do what?

00:05:05.772 --> 00:05:06.673
Oh.

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:08.808
Oh, for Josh Shapiro.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:11.511
Vote for John Fetterman.

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:13.913
Both the leaders who will fight for you

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:16.082
and your families.

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.116
Vote for folks

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:19.786
who will fight for that big inclusive,

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:21.421
hopeful, forward

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:24.090
looking America that we believe in.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.392
Who will work with Joe Biden

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.895
to build a country that is more fair

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:31.564
and more just and more equal

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.833
and more free?

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.234
That's our task.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.236
Let's get to work. I love your Philly.

